  "term": "somatic anxiety",
  "definition": "Somatic anxiety is the bodily or physical side of anxiety, considered as a dimension distinct from cognitive anxiety. In the source material, it is linked to subjective feelings of arousal and to psychophysiological responses across emotional situations.",
